D1 and D2 are now green. D3 still fails.
D3 failure is because when `distance == 0`, we don't reposition.
In D3:
`state.ball.x = brick.x + brick.w / 2;`
`state.ball.y = brick.y + brick.h / 2;`
`closestX = brick.x + brick.w / 2`.
`closestY = brick.y + brick.h / 2`.
`diffX = 0`, `diffY = 0`.
`distance = 0`.
The code goes to the `else` block and only flips `vy`. The ball remains at the center of the brick.

To fix this, we need a way to reposition even when the center is inside.
A simple way is to push the ball to the closest edge.

